# .browserslistrc
#
# Defines the browser support target for SWC (via next.config.js
# experimental.browsersListForSwc: true).
#
# These versions all support natively:
#   - Optional chaining (?.)
#   - Nullish coalescing (??)
#   - Logical assignment (&&=, ||=, ??=)
#   - async/await (no generator transform needed)
#   - Promise.allSettled / Promise.any
#   - String.replaceAll
#   - globalThis
#   - Dynamic import()
#   - CSS custom properties (vars)
#
# By listing only these modern versions, SWC skips the polyfill transforms
# for all of the above — saving ~25–35 KiB of JavaScript per page.
#
# If you need to support older browsers (e.g. Samsung Internet < 14,
# UC Browser, older iOS Safari), widen the targets below and re-measure
# with Lighthouse.

last 2 Chrome versions
last 2 Firefox versions
